# CNB Procfile — declares the launch processes buildpacks register.
#
# - web: production launch. heroku/go auto-registers this pointing
#   at the absolute path of the compiled binary
#   (/layers/heroku_go/go_target/bin/<module>).
# - dev: same as web for now. The Tilt extension's live_update
#   path-sync copies source files into /workspace on every save;
#   the running container keeps the existing binary until the next
#   pack rebuild. For a true sub-2s live recompile, add a Go
#   live-reload tool (e.g. air) via your own dev workflow:
#       go install github.com/air-verse/air@latest
#   and override `dev:` here to `air -c .air.toml`. We don't ship
#   that by default because the `tool` directive in go.mod (Go 1.24+)
#   that surfaces `air` for `go tool air` invocation breaks the
#   heroku/go buildpack's `web` process auto-registration with:
#       "tried to set web to default but it doesn't exist"
#   See web-go/go.mod's NOTE block for the trade-off.
web: bin/{{ .Name }}
dev: bin/{{ .Name }}
